<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article,</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Fantasy, musical, dark comedy</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Normal Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> - A small, portable phonograph made in 1950's which will play music whenever the stylus is placed over the turntable, irregardless of weather a record is there. The music played will resemble that of 1920's musical theatre unless a record is put in, in which case it will play the normal record.</p>
<p>- A large number of small woodland animals closely but not exactly matching those from northern Europe will spontaneously manifest in the areas surrounding the phonograph, and move onto the structure. When the record stops, they will disappear.</p>
<p>- The stylus of the phonograph moves up and down when no record is present, which can be decoded through binary into communications. These messages will repeat until a return message is sent by manually moving the stylus in the code.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> - Object is discovered in a police station after being confiscated.</p>
<p>- Foundation contains the object and soon realises the code and begins communicating with the object. The object says that her 'wicked godmother Annabelle' tried as hard as she could to get her out, and must have parylised and kidnapped her. She says she can't see anything and is confused. The foundation agents tell her that she has been turned into a phonograph. This prompts her to play a song called '<em>I used to be a princess, now I'm a record player!</em>'.</p>
<p>-They communicate further, and she says that she has to find a prince and take back the kingdom from 'the evil godmother Annabelle'. The foundation says she can't, but they will try to get back to the kingdom as the believe it holds anomalies. We then get an exploration log of the kingdom, as they arrive in the ruins of a large theatre. They move through the kingdom, which, while beautiful, is heavily damaged from a series of fires. They pass a civilian, and they ask where they can find the queen. The civilian asks them if they have been living under a rock, and says that a revolution has caused the queen to be beheaded. The foundation tells the object, and the final addendum is the song '<em>I can't go home, ever!</em>'</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Updated containment procedures show that investigations into the kingdom are ongoing.</p>
</div>
