			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829711">
									

<p>I think this could be a SCP or tale easily (and yes you can make a tale about an SCP entry that doesn’t exist on the mainlist)</p>
<p>But to make it work as a SCP you’ll have to differentiate with a narrative beyond just the person inside saying “please help me” and give exposition dumps</p>
<p>Two suggestions:<br />
1) expand the foundation’s research into this person the SCP is looking for, make that an adventure for the reader to go on</p>
<p>2) the ending won’t work as a stinger, in my opinion. Even if it’s really funny lyrics, the SCP complaining about being locked away just doesn’t seem to be a satisfying ending to me. I would try to think of something different.</p>
<p>(Also, I Don’t know what West Trancindentalia is but it sounds made up. I suggest making it a bit more grounded. Also&#8230; does that factor into the narrative at all? This diplomat I mean)</p>

