<blockquote>
<p>We then get an exploration log of the kingdom, as they arrive in the ruins of a large theatre. They move through the kingdom, which, while beautiful, is heavily damaged from a series of fires.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>So I am pretty confused here, what kingdom is this? is it some fictional universe or alternate dimension the foundation are traveling to? If there's no explanation how a magical fairytale kingdom exists in the same world as the foundation without somehow being obfuscated from the public, I will lose my immersion pretty much immediately.</em></p>
<p>I still suggest not using a fake country, unless it is some magical land explained in the article, for the same reason. The reason SCPs work (in my opinion) is that they're set in a realistic rendition of our world with the strange being hidden away&#8230; but a whole magical kingdom is gonna stretch my disbelief.</p>
<p>Now&#8230; This does not necessarily have to be the case in a tale, but even then, I feel like there's still some need to explain how this magical land has not been in our history forever.</p>
<p>I think this needs to be more grounded, personally.</p>

